- op: discuss  # 4cf6
  at: '2026-11-13T11:07:54Z'  # 4cf6
  by: agent  # 4cf6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4cf6
  clock: 4  # 4cf6
  nonce: 4cf6  # 4cf6
  message: "Fixed in PR #2168 (dev e46e89a9a8). Both causes: (1) the budget is now checked against the form that is written: token_budget.written_json_text / estimate_written_json_tokens (indent=2, sort_keys), pinned by a test that writes through safety_zones.user_out_open_json_dump and compares bytes; the shrink loop keeps an exact running size (compact._WrittenTierSize) and re-checks the finished map. (2) every tier records tier_tokens_used beside tier_tokens, so a file whose fixed sections exceed the budget says so. EVIDENCE, production path (hypergumbo survey, files read from disk, tokens = bytes // 4), three repositories that are not hypergumbo: alertmanager 4k 6854 used (1 node, over, reported), 16k 10323, 64k 56798; killbill 4k 13854 (1 node, over, reported), 16k 13814, 64k 58303; kserve 4k 8240 (1 node, over, reported), 16k 8227, 64k 58202. In all nine files tier_tokens_used equals bytes on disk // 4; all six 16k/64k files are within budget; all three 4k files are over and say so. A two-function repo: 4k 4189 used (limits alone is 2.8k tokens). Tests: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_tier_budget_written.py (53 cases; six mutations of what they pin each went red). Affected-test run 19,694 passed. NOT DONE HERE, moved to WI-lavum-sikag-hadir-gojiz-tarij-nirob-kirom-totik: the fixed sections are unchanged, so the 4k tier of every repository measured still holds one node; and the acceptance run showed a second loss, below."  # 4cf6
